IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `act-nouns`
IMPORT `act-interpretation-time`

-- Legislation Act 2001 (Australian Capital Territory), chapter 19 (the parts in scope): Part 19.1 Introductory, Part 19.2 Functions, Part 19.5 Service of documents.
--
-- When a served document is taken to be served (s 250) is in `act-interpretation-time.l4`, with the working-day rule it uses.
-- This module holds the rest: what "law" means in the chapter (s 195), how functions are given and exercised (ss 196 to 200),
-- to whom and how a document may be served (ss 245 to 249), and what the part leaves alone (ss 250 (2), 251, 252).
-- The definitions inside s 246 and s 250 (6) are also in `act-section-definitions.l4`.
--
-- A rule that says a document "may" be served in a way answers JUST TRUE when the facts match the way,
-- and NOTHING when they do not, because the text does not say that a document served some other way is not served (s 251 keeps other laws).

§ `Legislation Act 2001 (ACT): chapter 19, Parts 19.1, 19.2 and 19.5`

§§ `Part 19.1: Introductory`

-- src:2286 | In this chapter:
-- src:2287 | law means an Act, subordinate law or disallowable instrument.
@ref s 195 (src:2286-2287)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act or instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 195: the kind of document is a law for chapter 19` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a subordinate law` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a disallowable instrument` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a notifiable instrument` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a commencement notice` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a statutory instrument of another kind` THEN FALSE

§§ `Part 19.2: Functions`

-- src:2294 | (1) A provision of a law that gives a function to an entity also gives the entity the powers necessary and convenient to exercise the function.
@ref s 196 (1) (src:2294-2294)
GIVEN theProvisionGivesAFunctionToAnEntity IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 196 (1): the provision also gives the entity the powers necessary and convenient to exercise the function` MEANS theProvisionGivesAFunctionToAnEntity

-- src:2296 | (2) The powers given to the entity under subsection (1) are in addition to any other powers of the entity under the law.
@ref s 196 (2) (src:2296-2296)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 196 (2): the powers given under subsection (1) are in addition to any other powers of the entity under the law` MEANS TRUE

-- src:2299 | If a law gives a function to an entity, the function may be exercised from time to time.
@ref s 197 (src:2299-2299)
GIVEN aLawGivesAFunctionToAnEntity IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 197: the function may be exercised from time to time` MEANS aLawGivesAFunctionToAnEntity

-- src:2303 | (1) If a law authorises or requires a body to exercise a function, it may do so by resolution.
@ref s 199 (1) (src:2303-2303)
GIVEN aLawAuthorisesOrRequiresABodyToExerciseAFunction IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 199 (1): the body may exercise the function by resolution` MEANS aLawAuthorisesOrRequiresABodyToExerciseAFunction

-- src:2305 | (2) To remove any doubt, subsection (1) applies in relation to a function even though a law authorises or requires the function to be exercised in writing.
@ref s 199 (2) (src:2305-2305)
GIVEN aLawAuthorisesOrRequiresTheFunctionToBeExercisedInWriting IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 199 (2): subsection (1) applies to the function` MEANS TRUE

-- src:2306 | (3) If a law authorises or requires a signature by a person and the person is a body, the signature of a person authorised by the body for the purpose is taken to be the signature of the body.
@ref s 199 (3) (src:2306-2306)
GIVEN aLawAuthorisesOrRequiresASignatureByAPerson IS A BOOLEAN, thePersonIsABody IS A BOOLEAN, theSignerIsAuthorisedByTheBodyForThePurpose IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 199 (3): the signature of the person authorised by the body is taken to be the signature of the body` MEANS
    aLawAuthorisesOrRequiresASignatureByAPerson AND thePersonIsABody AND theSignerIsAuthorisedByTheBodyForThePurpose

-- src:2307 | (4) If a law gives a function to a body, the function may be exercised by the body as constituted for the time being.
@ref s 199 (4) (src:2307-2307)
GIVEN aLawGivesAFunctionToABody IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 199 (4): the function may be exercised by the body as constituted for the time being` MEANS aLawGivesAFunctionToABody

-- src:2310 | (5) The exercise of the function is not affected only because of vacancies in the body’s membership.
@ref s 199 (5) (src:2310-2310)
GIVEN theOnlyGroundIsVacanciesInTheBodysMembership IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199 (5): the exercise of the function is affected` MEANS
    IF   theOnlyGroundIsVacanciesInTheBodysMembership
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2311 | (6) Subsections (4) and (5) do not affect any quorum requirement applying to the body.
@ref s 199 (6) (src:2311-2311)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 199 (6): subsections (4) and (5) affect any quorum requirement applying to the body` MEANS FALSE

-- src:2314 | (7) If a body as constituted for the time being does something in exercise of a function given to the body under a law, the effect of the thing done by the body does not end only because the membership of the body changes.
@ref s 199 (7) (src:2314-2314)
GIVEN theOnlyGroundIsThatTheMembershipOfTheBodyChanges IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199 (7): the effect of the thing done by the body ends` MEANS
    IF   theOnlyGroundIsThatTheMembershipOfTheBodyChanges
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2316 | (8) Subsection (7) does not prevent the thing done by the body being ended or changed by the body as subsequently constituted for the time being.
@ref s 199 (8) (src:2316-2316)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 199 (8): subsection (7) prevents the thing done by the body being ended or changed by the body as subsequently constituted` MEANS FALSE

-- src:2319 | (1) If a law gives a function to the occupant of a position, the function may be exercised by the person for the time being occupying the position.
@ref s 200 (1) (src:2319-2319)
GIVEN aLawGivesAFunctionToTheOccupantOfAPosition IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 200 (1): the function may be exercised by the person for the time being occupying the position` MEANS aLawGivesAFunctionToTheOccupantOfAPosition

-- src:2321 | (2) If the person for the time being occupying a position does something in exercise of a function given to the occupant of the position under a law, the thing done by the person does not end only because the person ceases to be the occupant of the position.
@ref s 200 (2) (src:2321-2321)
GIVEN theOnlyGroundIsThatThePersonCeasesToBeTheOccupantOfThePosition IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 200 (2): the thing done by the person ends` MEANS
    IF   theOnlyGroundIsThatThePersonCeasesToBeTheOccupantOfThePosition
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2323 | (3) Subsection (2) does not prevent the thing done by the person being ended or changed by any person subsequently occupying the position for the time being.
@ref s 200 (3) (src:2323-2323)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 200 (3): subsection (2) prevents the thing done by the person being ended or changed by any person subsequently occupying the position` MEANS FALSE

§§ `Part 19.5: Service of documents`

-- src:2590 | This part applies to a document that is authorised or required under a law to be served (whether the word ‘serve’, ‘give’, ‘notify’, ‘send’ or ‘tell’ or any other word is used).
@ref s 245 (src:2590-2590)
GIVEN aDocumentIsAuthorisedOrRequiredUnderALawToBeServed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 245: this part applies to the document` MEANS aDocumentIsAuthorisedOrRequiredUnderALawToBeServed

DECLARE `Kind of entity served or serving` IS ONE OF
    `a corporation`
    `an agency that is an administrative unit`
    `an agency that is a statutory office-holder`
    `an agency constituted by 2 or more people`
    `any other agency`

DECLARE `Facts about a person and the entity` HAS
    `is concerned with, or takes part in, the management of the corporation or agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the director-general of the administrative unit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the occupant of the position` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is entitled, because of the position occupied, to preside at any meeting of the agency at which the person is present` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the chief executive officer (however described) of the agency` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2604 | executive officer means—
-- src:2605 | (a) for a corporation—a person (however described and whether or not the person is a director of the corporation) who is concerned with, or takes part in, the corporation’s management; or
-- src:2606 | (b) for an agency that is an administrative unit—the director-general of the administrative unit; or
-- src:2607 | (c) for an agency that is a statutory office-holder—the occupant of the position; or
-- src:2608 | (d) for an agency constituted by 2 or more people—the person who is entitled, because of the position occupied by the person, to preside at any meeting of the agency at which the person is present; or
-- src:2609 | (e) for any other agency—the chief executive officer (however described) of the agency; or
-- src:2610 | (f) for any agency—a person (however described) who is concerned with, or takes part in, the agency’s management.
@ref s 246, definition of executive officer (src:2604-2610)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of entity served or serving`, f IS A `Facts about a person and the entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 246: the person is an executive officer of the entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a corporation` THEN JUST management
    WHEN `an agency that is an administrative unit` THEN JUST (f's `is the director-general of the administrative unit` OR management)
    WHEN `an agency that is a statutory office-holder` THEN JUST (f's `is the occupant of the position` OR management)
    WHEN `an agency constituted by 2 or more people` THEN JUST (f's `is entitled, because of the position occupied, to preside at any meeting of the agency at which the person is present` OR management)
    WHEN `any other agency` THEN JUST (f's `is the chief executive officer (however described) of the agency` OR management)
    WHERE
        management MEANS f's `is concerned with, or takes part in, the management of the corporation or agency`

-- src:2595 | agency means—
-- src:2596 | (a) an administrative unit; or
-- src:2597 | (b) a statutory office-holder; or
-- src:2598 | (c) any other entity established for a public purpose under a law;
-- src:2599 | and includes a member of, or a member of the staff of, the agency.
@ref s 246, definition of agency (src:2595-2599)
GIVEN isAnAdministrativeUnit IS A BOOLEAN, isAStatutoryOfficeHolder IS A BOOLEAN, isAnotherEntityEstablishedForAPublicPurposeUnderALaw IS A BOOLEAN, isAMemberOfOrAMemberOfTheStaffOfTheAgency IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 246: the entity is an agency` MEANS
    isAnAdministrativeUnit OR isAStatutoryOfficeHolder OR isAnotherEntityEstablishedForAPublicPurposeUnderALaw OR isAMemberOfOrAMemberOfTheStaffOfTheAgency

-- src:2601 | corporation does not include an agency.
@ref s 246, definition of corporation (src:2601-2601)
GIVEN isACorporation IS A BOOLEAN, isAnAgency IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 246: the entity is a corporation for this part` MEANS isACorporation AND (NOT isAnAgency)

-- src:2602 | document includes a notice, an article that may be sent by post or anything else.
@ref s 246, definition of document (src:2602-2602)
GIVEN isANoticeAnArticleThatMayBeSentByPostOrAnythingElse IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 246: the thing is a document` MEANS
    IF   isANoticeAnArticleThatMayBeSentByPostOrAnythingElse
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The facts about how a document was delivered that ss 247 to 249 look at.
-- A field that a particular section does not look at is not read by that section's rule.
DECLARE `Facts about how a document was served` HAS
    `it was given to the person to be served, or to an executive officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was sent by prepaid post, addressed as the section requires, to an address the section allows` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was faxed to a fax number of the person to be served` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was emailed to an email address of the person to be served` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was left, addressed as the section requires, at an address the section allows` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the apparent age in years of the person it was left with` IS A NUMBER
    `the person it was left with appears to live or be employed at the address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person it was left with appears to be employed at the address` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2616 | (1) A document may be served on an individual—
-- src:2617 | (a) by giving it to the individual; or
-- src:2618 | (b) by sending it by prepaid post, addressed to the individual, to a home or business address of the individual; or
-- src:2619 | (c) by faxing it to a fax number of the individual; or
-- src:2620 | (d) by emailing it to an email address of the individual; or
-- src:2621 | (e) by leaving it, addressed to the individual, at a home or business address of the individual with someone who appears to be at least 16 years old and to live or be employed at the address.
@ref s 247 (1) (src:2616-2621)
GIVEN how IS A `How a document is served`, f IS A `Facts about how a document was served`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 247 (1): the document may be served on an individual in this way` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `by giving it to the person, or to an executive officer` THEN
        IF   f's `it was given to the person to be served, or to an executive officer`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by sending it by prepaid post` THEN
        IF   f's `it was sent by prepaid post, addressed as the section requires, to an address the section allows`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by fax` THEN
        IF   f's `it was faxed to a fax number of the person to be served`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by email` THEN
        IF   f's `it was emailed to an email address of the person to be served`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by leaving it at an address with someone there` THEN
        IF   f's `it was left, addressed as the section requires, at an address the section allows`
             AND f's `the apparent age in years of the person it was left with` AT LEAST 16
             AND f's `the person it was left with appears to live or be employed at the address`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2626 | (1) A document may be served on a corporation—
-- src:2627 | (a) by giving it to an executive officer of the corporation; or
-- src:2628 | (b) by sending it by prepaid post, addressed to the corporation (or an executive officer of the corporation), to the address of any of its registered offices or any other business address of the corporation; or
-- src:2629 | (c) by faxing it to a fax number of the corporation; or
-- src:2630 | (d) by emailing it to an email address of the corporation; or
-- src:2631 | (e) by leaving it, addressed to the corporation (or an executive officer of the corporation), at the address of any of the corporation’s registered offices, or any other business address of the corporation, with someone who appears to be at least 16 years old and to be employed at the address.
@ref s 248 (1) (src:2626-2631)
GIVEN how IS A `How a document is served`, f IS A `Facts about how a document was served`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 248 (1): the document may be served on a corporation in this way` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `by giving it to the person, or to an executive officer` THEN
        IF   f's `it was given to the person to be served, or to an executive officer`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by sending it by prepaid post` THEN
        IF   f's `it was sent by prepaid post, addressed as the section requires, to an address the section allows`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by fax` THEN
        IF   f's `it was faxed to a fax number of the person to be served`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by email` THEN
        IF   f's `it was emailed to an email address of the person to be served`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by leaving it at an address with someone there` THEN
        IF   f's `it was left, addressed as the section requires, at an address the section allows`
             AND f's `the apparent age in years of the person it was left with` AT LEAST 16
             AND f's `the person it was left with appears to be employed at the address`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2636 | A document may be served on an agency—
-- src:2637 | (a) by giving it to an executive officer of the agency; or
-- src:2638 | (b) by sending it by prepaid post, addressed to the agency (or an executive officer of the agency), to the address of any office of the agency or any other business address of the agency; or
-- src:2639 | (c) by faxing it to a fax number of the agency; or
-- src:2640 | (d) by emailing it to an email address of the agency; or
-- src:2641 | (e) by leaving it, addressed to the agency (or an executive officer of the agency), at the address of any of the agency’s offices or any other business address of the agency with someone who appears to be employed at the agency.
@ref s 249 (src:2636-2641)
GIVEN how IS A `How a document is served`, f IS A `Facts about how a document was served`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 249: the document may be served on an agency in this way` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `by giving it to the person, or to an executive officer` THEN
        IF   f's `it was given to the person to be served, or to an executive officer`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by sending it by prepaid post` THEN
        IF   f's `it was sent by prepaid post, addressed as the section requires, to an address the section allows`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by fax` THEN
        IF   f's `it was faxed to a fax number of the person to be served`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by email` THEN
        IF   f's `it was emailed to an email address of the person to be served`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by leaving it at an address with someone there` THEN
        IF   f's `it was left, addressed as the section requires, at an address the section allows`
             AND f's `the person it was left with appears to be employed at the address`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2623 | (2) This section applies to service of a document outside the ACT in the same way as it applies to service of the document in the ACT.
@ref s 247 (2) (src:2623-2623)
GIVEN theDocumentIsServedOutsideTheACT IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 247 (2): the section applies to the service in the same way as it applies to service in the ACT` MEANS TRUE

-- src:2633 | (2) This section applies to service of a document outside the ACT in the same way as it applies to service of the document in the ACT.
@ref s 248 (2) (src:2633-2633)
GIVEN theDocumentIsServedOutsideTheACT IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 248 (2): the section applies to the service in the same way as it applies to service in the ACT` MEANS TRUE

-- src:2646 | (2) However, subsection (1) does not affect the operation of the Evidence Act 2011, section 160 (Postal articles).
@ref s 250 (2) (src:2646-2646)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 250 (2): subsection (1) affects the operation of the Evidence Act 2011, section 160 (Postal articles)` MEANS FALSE

-- src:2659 | (1) This part does not affect the operation of any other law that authorises or requires service of a document otherwise than as provided under this part.
@ref s 251 (1) (src:2659-2659)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251 (1): this part affects the operation of any other law that authorises or requires service of a document otherwise than as provided under this part` MEANS FALSE

-- src:2660 | (2) Despite this part, a law (or, if the law is an Act, a regulation under the Act) may provide—
-- src:2661 | (a) that a document of a particular kind may or must be served (however described) only in a particular way or to a particular address or number; or
@ref s 251 (2) (a) (src:2660-2661)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251 (2) (a): a law may provide that a document of a particular kind may or must be served only in a particular way or to a particular address or number` MEANS TRUE

-- src:2662 | (b) for the date (or date and time) when service (however described) of a document is taken to have been made.
@ref s 251 (2) (b) (src:2662-2662)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251 (2) (b): a law may provide for the date, or date and time, when service of a document is taken to have been made` MEANS TRUE

-- src:2665 | This part does not affect the power of a court or tribunal to authorise or require service of a document otherwise than as provided under this part.
@ref s 252 (src:2665-2665)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 252: this part affects the power of a court or tribunal to authorise or require service of a document otherwise than as provided under this part` MEANS FALSE
